  "term": "niacin",
  "definition": "In this psychiatric diagnostic context, niacin refers to the substance used to measure the niacin skin-flushing response, a bodily reaction being studied as an objective biomarker for identifying mental disorders. The packet supports this testing-related meaning rather than a broader general definition of niacin.",
